// The terminal interface: the keymap the app binds and, later, the screen it
// installs it on. Package ui is every ui/*.salam file merged; this file is the
// entry point. It holds no code of its own.
//
//   keymap.salam  Command, and Vim(sink): the basalam vim preset plus the four
//                 application keys (space, n, p, :)
//   shell.salam   Shell: the one Screen, the root Row/Stack/Row tree, the four
//                 focus stops in ring order, and the refit and hint ladder
//   loop.salam    Run: the one event loop — dispatch a key, apply the verbs it
//                 reported, paint.
//   terminal.salam
//                 RestoreSequence, InstallGuard, Begin, End: the bytes and the
//                 flag file that put the terminal back on every exit path.
//
// Imports basalam and nothing from the player: the keymap reports verbs to a
// callback, so the interface layer does not know what playback is.

package ui
